&lt;p&gt;Do you follow every shift in digital marketing, media and commerce, and always have a view on which stories matter the most?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you want to create content across channels that educates the next generation of marketers?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Does the idea of shaping the content for one of digital marketing&#39;s longest-running publications excite you?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If so, we&#39;d love to hear from you!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fospha is the measurement system enterprise retail and ecommerce brands run their business on. We give marketing teams one clear, daily view of what&#39;s actually working — across every channel and everywhere they sell, from their website to Amazon and TikTok Shop — down to the level of a single ad or piece of creative. It replaces guesswork and gut feel with a number marketing, finance and agencies can all trust and act on. Brands including Dyson, Gymshark, and Lululemon use Fospha up to 25 times a day to decide where budget should move next. We&#39;ve spent over a decade building this, with more than $40 billion in marketing spend now optimised through the platform — and we&#39;re scaling fast across London, Mumbai and Austin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About ClickZ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://clickz.com/&quot;&gt;ClickZ&lt;/a&gt; is Fospha&#39;s media partner and one of the world&#39;s longest-running digital marketing publications, trusted by CMOs and senior marketers since 1997. Its focus is how measurement shapes marketing decisions, and it covers the wider marketing that measurement informs. Readers come to ClickZ to understand:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How marketing leaders build teams, explain results to finance and earn influence in the room&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retail and commerce marketing, including retail media and marketplaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How AI, search and ad platform changes affect planning and results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where to invest across brand, creative, performance, affiliate and influencer marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How brands measure performance, from attribution and incrementality to mix modelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a permanent role at the heart of ClickZ. You&#39;ll run the day-to-day content engine: spotting the stories that matter to marketing leaders, turning them into sharp content across email, social and the website, and growing the audience that reads it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work is varied. In a single week you might cover a session at a major commerce event, publish a piece on a platform change, prepare a leadership Q&amp;amp;A, and review a stack of contributor pitches. You&#39;ll also build ClickZ&#39;s network of event partners, contributors, PR contacts and industry leaders, and meet many of them in person at industry events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with ClickZ&#39;s lead, who sets the brand&#39;s strategy, and you&#39;ll have real ownership of your workstreams from the start. This is an &lt;strong&gt;office-based role&lt;/strong&gt; in London.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role suits someone with a journalist&#39;s instinct for a story, a marketer&#39;s eye for an audience, and the energy to keep both going every week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll work on&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your time will be spread across three areas, with content creation at the core. All three serve one goal: growing the ClickZ brand and getting its content to more of the right people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Focus area&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it covers&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Content creation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The core of the role: editorial content on market trends, event coverage, brand leadership interviews and Q&amp;amp;As, flagship newsletters, and social content&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Audience growth and content analysis&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Growing ClickZ&#39;s readership and subscribers, testing new formats, and using performance data to decide what to create next&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Network and community&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Building relationships with event partners, marketing and commerce leaders, PR teams and contributors, online and in person at industry events&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the content engine fed.&lt;/strong&gt; Track the news and trends that matter to marketing and commerce leaders, and turn them into timely, well-argued content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar on every channel.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring a creative eye to email, social and web content, and build a distinct content plan for each channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the flagship newsletters.&lt;/strong&gt; Draft and refine ClickZ&#39;s flagship newsletters, and develop more tailored formats for different parts of the audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring leadership conversations to life.&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare and support podcast and Q&amp;amp;A conversations with leaders across marketing and commerce, and, with training and support, grow into hosting them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow the audience.&lt;/strong&gt; Work out which formats and topics readers respond to, and turn readers into subscribers. Design campaigns that bring back readers who&#39;ve gone quiet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Let data inform the calls.&lt;/strong&gt; Track what content delivers, use the numbers to decide what to do next, and share what&#39;s working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the first filter.&lt;/strong&gt; Review PR pitches and contributor submissions, and pick out the strong and relevant ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the network.&lt;/strong&gt; Reach out to contributors, speakers and event partners, grow an always-on contributor community, and build lasting relationships with PR teams and industry leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get out into the industry.&lt;/strong&gt; Attend events, support event partnerships, and find new events worth ClickZ&#39;s time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work agentically.&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI tools to speed up research, drafting and multimedia content, while owning the quality of what goes out.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What are we looking for?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We hire for potential and taste. You should apply if you meet these six must-haves:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have around one year of experience creating content in the digital marketing, media or commerce world, whether in journalism, editorial, content or social roles (internships, placements and personal projects count), and a genuine passion for digital marketing and commerce, and for the leaders shaping them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have &lt;strong&gt;strong editorial judgement&lt;/strong&gt;: you can tell good content from weak, and relevant from noise, and you know a big story when you see one (experience of writing, editing or curating, including student or personal publications)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a &lt;strong&gt;creative eye to content&lt;/strong&gt; across email, social and web, with a feel for multimedia formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are &lt;strong&gt;audience-minded&lt;/strong&gt;: you think about who&#39;s reading, how to reach more of the right people and how to build a community around a brand. You&#39;re also comfortable with data: you use performance numbers to make content decisions and back up your conclusions (experience using analytics such as GA4)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are &lt;strong&gt;agentically minded&lt;/strong&gt;: you love experimenting with new tools for multimedia content creation and adaptation, and know when to push them and when to take over&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are &lt;strong&gt;a natural conversationalist&lt;/strong&gt;: you get a guest talking, hold your own with senior leaders, and leave an event with new connections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Also important:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have &lt;strong&gt;high agency&lt;/strong&gt;: you take ownership of your work, stretch beyond the brief and challenge the status quo when something could be better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy a fast-paced, innovative startup environment, where you&#39;ll ship quickly, iterate often and juggle several projects at once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are happy to travel for industry events, within the UK and occasionally overseas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Values and Principles&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be able to demonstrate examples of our core principles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seek inclusion &amp;amp; diversity:&lt;/strong&gt; We create an environment where everyone feels welcome, and people are encouraged to speak and be heard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Hard, Work Well, Work Together:&lt;/strong&gt; We take responsibility for making things happen, independently and together; we help colleagues in need and close loops, making sure our work is complete and has lasting impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow:&lt;/strong&gt; We are proactive, curious and unafraid of failure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer at the heart:&lt;/strong&gt; We care about the customer, feel their pain and love building product that solves their biggest problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candour with caring:&lt;/strong&gt; We deliver candid feedback with kindness and receive it with gratitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary: £34k + discretionary 10% bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of content for a media brand that has covered digital marketing for nearly 30 years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Early ownership of your workstreams, and the chance to shape how modern marketers learn and make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A growing network across PR teams, contributors and industry leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on podcast experience, with regular conversations with leaders across marketing and commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A place at major industry events, with a front-row view of commerce, media and digital marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a leading global venture builder, &lt;a href=&quot;https://blenheimchalcot.com/blog&quot;&gt;Blenheim Chalcot&lt;/a&gt;, and learn from the incredible talent in BC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The right mix of challenges, learning and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A workplace pension, through Royal London, with Fospha matching your contributions up to 3%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A £1,000/year flexible benefits allowance to put towards private medical insurance, dental cover, a health cash plan, gym membership, extra holiday, or a pension top-up - whatever suits you!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Wellhub, giving you one membership across gyms, boutique studios, and wellbeing apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days&#39; annual leave plus 8 UK bank holidays, an extra day off for your birthday! and more holiday the longer you stay (26 days after 3 years, 27 after 6)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life assurance worth 4x your annual salary, from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle to Work scheme, plus discounts on everyday spending through our benefits portal — Apple, Tesco, IKEA, M&amp;amp;S, Deliveroo, cinema tickets and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly one-to-one sessions with a financial adviser, plus access to payroll-deducted loans through Salary Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid volunteering days each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular socials, free weekly snacks, and Lunch &amp;amp; Learn events at our Scale Space office, plus access to the wider Blenheim Chalcot community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to travel — including to our India and North America offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Top tip: Share two or three pieces of content you&#39;re proud of, and tell us one story ClickZ should cover next, and why.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;By submitting your CV you understand that we have a legitimate interest to use your personal data for the purposes of assessing your eligibility for this role.&amp;nbsp; This means that we may use your personal data to contact you to discuss your CV or arrange an interview, or transfer your CV to the hiring manager(s) of the role you have applied for.&amp;nbsp; You can ask us at any time to remove your CV from our database by emailing&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- but please note that this means we will no longer consider you for the role you have applied for.&amp;nbsp;You can review our privacy policy&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.blenheimchalcot.com/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT NEXGEN CLOUD:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NexGen Cloud is the company behind Hyperstack, a full-stack AI cloud serving tens of thousands of customers from AI researchers to enterprises running the world&#39;s most compute-intensive workloads. We deliver on-demand and private GPU infrastructure to teams who treat performance as a requirement, not a feature.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a tight-knit, fast-moving team working at the cutting edge of AI cloud infrastructure. We practice what we preach, equipping our people with AI at every level so we can solve harder problems, ship faster, and keep raising the bar for what enterprise GPU infrastructure looks like.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE: Senior Business Development Manager – Vertical Markets&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hyperstack already runs production GPU capacity at scale for AI start-ups, AI service providers and enterprise AI teams. This role exists to extend that position into compute-intensive, regulated and specialist industries — financial services, healthcare and life sciences, robotics and autonomous systems, computer vision and industrial AI — where compute budgets are already committed and infrastructure partners are being chosen now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own a named vertical end to end: the demand thesis, the target account map, the outbound motion, and every deal through to signature. This is a full-cycle role with real ownership, not a top-of-funnel handoff — you&#39;ll become the recognised commercial authority for your vertical inside NexGen, and a credible presence in that industry externally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Role positioning: this is a role for a senior seller who already holds trust in a compute-intensive industry and wants full ownership of turning that trust into a book of business — the strategy, the pipeline and the close.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BE DOING:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rather than a long checklist, here&#39;s what success in this role looks like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a named vertical end to end — build the demand thesis, size the addressable market, and turn it into a prioritised target account map&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-source the majority of your own pipeline and reach the people who decide compute budget: CIO, CTO, Chief Data or AI Officer, and the procurement and risk functions that gate them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical discovery to a real specification, then own the full cycle to signature — commercial proposal, security review, procurement, legal and MSA negotiation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure multi-year committed reservations and on-demand entry points, and keep a forecast the business can plan capacity against&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Hyperstack&#39;s presence in your vertical — industry events, analyst and partner relationships, reference customers and case studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed vertical requirements into Product, Capacity and Marketing with enough specificity to change decisions, then follow through until they land&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the internal reference point for your vertical — brief the wider Sales team and raise the technical floor around you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT YOU:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re more interested in how you think and work than in a perfect CV. You&#39;ll likely bring a combination of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in business development, enterprise sales or solution sales, including at least 3 years carrying a new business number in complex enterprise environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrable record of opening net-new enterprise logos from a standing start — self-sourced, not inherited and not renewal-led&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep credibility in at least one compute-intensive vertical — financial services, healthcare and life sciences, robotics and autonomous systems, computer vision and industrial AI, media and entertainment, or engineering and simulation — including an active network at buying level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantive infrastructure fluency (cloud, IaaS, HPC, data centre, GPU or AI compute), or a proven history of learning a technical domain to the point of holding your own with engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of closing complex deals through procurement, security review and legal, with contract values and cycle lengths you can talk to in detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a neo-cloud, GPU-as-a-Service platform, hyperscaler or HPC infrastructure vendor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior ownership of a vertical or industry go-to-market as a named remit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulated buying environments — data residency and sovereignty, isolation requirements, and the security and compliance reviews that come with them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling committed capacity or reservation-style contracts rather than pure consumption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formal sales methodology — MEDDPICC, Command of the Message or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base salary with uncapped commission and accelerators above target, plus equity participation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee wellbeing benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of holiday, plus public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working, with Tuesday to Thursday in the London office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real ownership of a named vertical, with the trust to build and run it as your own&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear route to principal-level individual contribution or vertical leadership as your vertical scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, international culture built on trust, transparency, and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to help shape NexGen Cloud&#39;s team, culture, and future alongside ambitious, mission-driven colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MORE INFORMATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Head over to our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nexgencloud.com/careers?utm_medium=organic&amp;amp;utm_source=google&quot;&gt;NexGen Cloud&lt;/a&gt; careers page to view current openings and follow us on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/nexgen-cloud&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/CloudNexgen&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our journey, newest releases and hear exciting news in the neocloud space.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT NEXGEN CLOUD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NexGen Cloud is a fast-growing GPU cloud and AI infrastructure business. We&#39;re the company behind Hyperstack — a self-serve, on-demand cloud platform built for high-performance AI, HPC, and compute-heavy workloads. Powered by 100% renewable energy and NVIDIA architecture, Hyperstack gives teams from AI startups to enterprise the compute they need, without the cost or complexity of legacy cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We move fast, solve hard problems, and build things that matter. If you want ownership, real impact, and a front-row seat to one of the most consequential infrastructure shifts of the decade — this is the place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE: Data Analyst&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NexGen Cloud is moving to a data-driven way of running the business. Right now, revenue, occupancy, billing and pipeline data live across data warehouses, business systems and APIs, and the numbers don&#39;t always agree. We&#39;re building out our Strategic Finance team so that leadership, sales and operations can rely on one set of figures and act on them daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role suits someone who enjoys the technical craft of data and wants to learn the commercial side of the AI compute market. We&#39;ll teach you that context. When a number looks wrong, you&#39;ll dig until you find why, and you&#39;ll come back with a fix as well as the problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BE DOING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rather than a checklist, here&#39;s what success in this role actually looks like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the pipelines that bring data from across the business into Databricks and Power BI, and automate the manual steps along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the daily revenue and occupancy reporting that leadership uses to track how the GPU fleet is performing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check that what we bill matches what customers actually used, covering power draw, utilisation, asset registers and credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support commission calculations and give sales leadership a clear view of pipeline health, conversion and churn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model pricing options and deal economics so investment decisions are grounded in real numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate every figure before it reaches leadership or anyone outside the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the wider team work confidently with BI tools and data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT YOU&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care more about how you think and work than a perfect CV. You&#39;ll likely bring a combination of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience as a Data Analyst or in a similar role, including data extraction, integration or automation projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL and Excel skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid Power BI experience, including reconciling figures when different sources disagree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on use of a CRM (HubSpot or similar), and of AI tools to speed up analysis and build work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A root-cause mindset: you find the underlying cause rather than reporting the symptom, and you bring a proposed solution with it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Databricks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to billing, revenue assurance or commission processes, ideally in a cloud, SaaS or usage-based business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some experience with financial modelling or FP&amp;amp;A work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time spent in a high-growth company where data processes were still being built&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and annual discretionary bonus scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee wellbeing benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days holiday, plus public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Pension Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working arrangements (remote or hybrid, depending on role and location)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real ownership and autonomy — the trust to take initiative and experiment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Visible, meaningful impact as we scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear career progression in a high-growth company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, international culture built on trust, transparency, and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to help shape NexGen Cloud&#39;s team, culture, and future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHY APPLY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from all backgrounds. If you enjoy solving complex infrastructure problems and want to build something meaningful at scale, we&#39;d like to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
